			<div class="content" id="post-content-4857547">
									

<p>This really did very little for me, despite my expectations going in. The central story behind this article is one that's been told many, many times before &#8212; and this article didn't delve any deeper into it than any other stories have in the past. I see no attempt here to truly humanize Gabriel McQueen &#8212; he's just a walking mental-illness stereotype whose descent into murderous frenzy is never really built up or justified until a paragraph before shit goes down. The scenes of incredible violence in this are all too gratuitous and over-the-top to take seriously, and the actions and behaviour of McQueen in those scenes are reminiscent of a b-list slasher movie.</p>
<p>Also an issue for me are the multiple errors in grammar (for example - the apostrophe in &quot;lifts&quot; in &quot;McQueen lift's Laura&quot;), style (always referring to characters by their first names in the recording logs), and the choppy and somewhat stilted structure of the syntax, which along with the over-the-top scenes of unnecessary and graphic violence made this hard to get through.</p>
<p>Lastly (and this may not be up to me to decide, but it's only my opinion), the content of this article seems to sharply contrast with the initial prompt behind it. While the initial anomaly of the article follows the subtlety and quiet emotion suggested by the prompt quite well, it quickly becomes an afterthought as the story of the article devolves into a slasher movie in SCP form.</p>
<p>I started reading this article expecting something incredible, and left sorely disappointed. Downvote.</p>

