<p>Greetings. Let me go through this, as you've presented:</p>
<div class="collapsible-block">
<div class="collapsible-block-folded"><a class="collapsible-block-link" href="javascript:;">+&nbsp;show&nbsp;block</a></div>
<div class="collapsible-block-unfolded" style="display:none">
<div class="collapsible-block-unfolded-link"><a class="collapsible-block-link" href="javascript:;">–&nbsp;hide&nbsp;block</a></div>
<div class="collapsible-block-content">
<p><strong>truly humanize Gabriel McQueen:</strong> The entirety of Addendum 1 was meant to do exactly this. In fact, a whopping majority of the article is spent characterizing McQueen, going into his personal life and his struggles growing up. I have no clue as to how else to characterize him without dumping thousands of more words into the article, causing it drag along moreso than it maybe has already.</p>
<p><strong>a b-list slasher:</strong> since you don't necessarily state the criteria for this, I have no clue how to correct it. The log itself has already been reduced via the lack of sound, which was intended to subvert this problem. The only thing readers get to see is purely the visual feed, which in my opinion seems pretty realistic? I don't understand where it falls from feeling real to &quot;being like a crappy film.&quot; I can almost see the mention of Laura in a bath towel being a potential source of the problem, so I have removed it. However, I would like to ask what you'd do in this situation presented? How could I detract it less from sounding like this?</p>
<p><strong>walking mental-illness stereotype</strong>: Frankly I don't necessarily know where this stems from. The only part of McQueen where I could potentially see potential stereotyping is the mention of medication for anger-related problems. I have since removed this, but otherwise I'm unsure of where else this occurs. I tried as best as I could to keep mentions or anything of explicit mental health problems at a minimum to avoid this. As to the part where you mentioned that his killings were unjustified: I'd have to argue against this. Its hinted several times that McQueen was somewhat unstable, even directly admitting to torturing animals (which is an indication of underlying tendencies). Also, just logically speaking, how fast do you think you'd confront a cheating spouse? I feel as if it would be unrealistic to elongate McQueens confrontation, especially given the context that he had hidden cameras all over the house. In this regard, I simply have no solution.</p>
<p><strong>multiple errors in grammar:</strong> These are being corrected, but currently I'm working ;-;</p>
<p><strong>article devolves:</strong> I cite my earlier comment of the &quot;b-slasher movie&quot; to be vague. I simply don't understand nor know how to fix this. Not only that, but the contrast was intended ([&#8230;] that has changed a once innocuous place into something…else). I specifically wanted there to be a sharp contrast in order for the ending to be more surprising for the reader. But, still, this is a valid critique. I'm unsure of how to fix it though.</p>
<p><strong>despite my expectations going in:</strong> this doesn't necessarily seem like a problem tied to the article. In truth, this seems a bit unfair. I have no way to defend against pre-conceived expectations, especially considering that this story wasn't meant to &quot;awe-dropping.&quot; It was intended to be personal, to have an emotional connection amongst a small group of people. In my opinion, downvoting an article based off prior expectations seems somewhat unreasonable. (This isn't to suggest that that's what you did, just in general)</p>
</div>
</div>
</div>
<p>I really do appreciate your comments. I will try to address them in a decent manner. I'll edit this comment once they've been implemented. Thank you!</p>

